// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 144: Action rand-qualified fields (page 213)
struct S1 {
  rand bit[3:0]   a;
  bit[3:0]        b;
}
struct S2 {
  rand S1         s1_1;
  S1              s1_2;
}
action A {
  rand bit[3:0]   a;
}
action B {
  A  a_1, a_2;
  rand bit[3:0]   b;

  activity {
    a_1;
    a_2;
  }
}

Example 145 shows an action-qualified field in action B named a_bit. The PSS processing tool assigns a
value to a_bit when it is traversed in the activity body. The semantics are identical to assigning a
value to the rand-qualified action field A::a.
